    "https://www.bridgewater.edu/careers/": {
      "title": "Careers",
      "description": "Careers | Employment Opportunities | Bridgewater College Skip to content Academics Degrees and Programs Graduate Programs Academic Support Career Development Research Academic Calendar Faculty Finder Forrer Learning Commons Study Abroad & Away Admissions & Aid How to Visit How to Apply Tuition and Costs Financial Aid Bienvenido a Bridgewater College For First-Year Students For Graduate Students For Transfer Students For International Students Admitted Students Life at Bridgewater Housing & Residence Life Dining Services Health and Wellness Campus Safety Clubs and Organizations Student Resources Campus Events Calendar Visit More Apply Athletics Alumni Events Newsroom Give Campus Store Careers & Employment Community Members Directory About BC myBC 🔒 Search Careers Working together for the future Interested in a career at Bridgewater College? Find current jobs listings and benefits of employment. BC is a private liberal arts college, founded in 1880. We’re committed to furthering a long-standing tradition of excellence in everything we do. If you want to know more, check out our mission and goals and history . Come join us and be part of the next phase in BC history. Employment Opportunities View current job opportunities and apply for open positions. Current Job Openings Great Employee Benefits Bridgewater College currently provides its employees with a comprehensive range of benefits, including a generous paid time off (PTO) policy, 403(b) retirement plan, tuition remission program, paid parental leave, health and dental benefits, life insurance, disability benefits, employee assistance plan (EAP) and paid holidays. Benefits of Employment Close-Knit Community Faculty and staff at Bridgewater College are part of a close-knit community. We care about one another and welcome everyone, no matter where you’re from. You can walk across campus in just a few minutes. It’s easy to get to know your colleagues and the students. You’ll have the opportunity to gather at departmental and office events, as well as campus-wide gatherings for employees. A Community Like No Other Watch this video on YouTube All about Location The nearby communities of the Shenandoah Valley, including the town of Bridgewater, the cities of Harrisonburg and Staunton, and the counties of Rockingham and Augusta, are great places to live and raise a family, with strong school systems and low crime rates. Bridgewater & Surrounding Areas Onboarding for New Employees Starting a new role comes with a lot to learn, and our Onboarding for New Employees webpage is designed to make that process clear and manageable. It guides new hires from the moment they accept their offer through the end of their first year, helping them feel confident and connected within the Bridgewater College community. This resource supports a smooth transition by providing: A clear, step-by-step overview of the onboarding journey. Direct links to essential platforms and documents to enhance ease of use. A user-friendly layout that highlights important procedures and available campus resources. With everything in one place, new employees can easily find what they need, understand expectations, and prepare for each stage of their first year. Onboarding for New Employees Launch Experience Get to Know the Campus Nothing beats coming to campus but you can sneak a peek at our centers, classrooms, dining hall, fitness facility and more on our online virtual tour. See for yourself what BC has to offer. Explore Now Transparency in Coverage Posting Your Rights and Protections Against Surprise Medical Bills (pdf download) Medical Insurance Transparency in Coverage (TIC) Federal and State Employment Law Posters Federal & VA Employment Laws Poster – English Federal & VA Employment Laws Poster – Spanish Family and Medical Leave Act Poster Fair Labor Standards Act Poster Colorado Employment Laws Poster Florida Employment Laws Poster Maryland Employment Laws Poster Colorado Whistleblower Laws Poster EEOC 2023 USDA And Justice for All Poster Veterans Resources Right to Work Poster EVerify Participation Poster E-Verify Notice of Participation Department of Justice Right to Work Notice Job Openings Current full-time, part-time and temporary jobs on faculty, staff, administration and work study. Benefits of Employment BC’s benefit program is designed to care for you and your family by continually exploring innovative options that offer security and support employees’ unique needs. Bridgewater & Surrounding Areas Bridgewater’s backyard is one of the most scenic areas in the nation. The Shenandoah Valley. Expansive farmland with a backdrop of mountains on both sides. Onboarding for New Employees We are dedicated to supporting new employees with the resources and guidance they need for a successful transition. This timeline outlines key steps and important… Student Employment at BC Looking to work on campus? Learn more about student employment positions available on campus. Non-Discrimination Notice Bridgewater College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, sex, marital status, disability, religion, age, veteran status, family medical… Request Info Apply Now Visit Want to learn more? Loading... Congratulations! You are one step closer to discovering if Bridgewater College may be the right fit for you. We are excited to work with you as you decide where you want to continue your educational journey. Schedule a Visit First Year Student Transfer Student Graduate Student Returning Student Experience Life at BC A visit to campus is the first step in determining if Bridgewater is the right fit for you. That’s when you’ll see what life at BC is really like. Schedule a Visit Virtual Tour bridgewater-logo 402 East College Street Bridgewater, Virginia 22812 540-828-8000 Admission & Aid Visit Apply Careers myBC Campus Police Accessibility HEERF Reporting Legal Title IX Hazing Prohibition & Adam's Law Non-Discrimination Notice Annual 